================================================================================
NOTICES AND ARCHITECTURE BOUNDARIES
================================================================================

1. First-Party Workspaces (Apache-2.0)
   - `apps/web`: Next.js 16 (App Router) unified workspace housing 52 local
     PDF & Media tools, on-device RAG, semantic intent routing, and Voice Orb UI.
   - `apps/desktop`: Electron 35 local desktop workstation (`MUXARO-Studio-Windows-x64.exe`).
   - `apps/mobile`: Capacitor 7 Android application (`MUXARO-Studio.apk`).
   - `apps/api` & `apps/media-worker`: Fastify 5 self-hostable REST/SSE API and
     media processing microservice.
   - `packages/*` & `security/`: Shared contracts, entitlements, source adapters,
     and defense-in-depth security utilities.

2. Out-of-Process Native & WebAssembly Tool Boundaries
   MUXARO invokes external native binaries and WebAssembly workers strictly
   out-of-process without statically or dynamically linking copyleft libraries
   into first-party TypeScript/Java sources:

   - FFmpeg / FFprobe (`https://ffmpeg.org/`)
     Executed as external child processes (`execFile` / `spawn`, `shell: false`)
     in `apps/desktop` and `apps/api`, and inside sandboxed browser Web Workers
     via `@ffmpeg/ffmpeg` (MIT) and `@ffmpeg/core` (LGPL-2.1+ / GPL-2.0+
     depending on build flags). Distributed Windows releases that bundle
     `ffmpeg.exe` comply with upstream FFmpeg source-offer and attribution
     notices documented in `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`.

   - yt-dlp (`https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp`)
     Licensed under The Unlicense; invoked strictly out-of-process in
     `apps/desktop` and `apps/api` or used for stream metadata inspection.

   - Local AI & Speech Tooling (`@huggingface/transformers`, `whisper.cpp`, `Piper`, `Ollama`)
     `@huggingface/transformers` is licensed under Apache-2.0; optional user-installed
     offline Voice Packs (`whisper.cpp` MIT, `Piper` MIT) and local LLMs (`Ollama` MIT)
     are downloaded/executed separately on user request in app data storage.

